; D8-v2 lowered-tree materialization: the emitted form's expression
; default fails to evaluate.
;
; `sugar` lowers via test/identity-v1, which emits `sugar-normal` by
; convention. The hook copies declared kvpairs from the source —
; sugar declares no keys, so the emitted form has no kvpairs.
; sugar-normal.x has `:default (nope)`, where `nope` is a declared
; expr-func with no `:impl`. The lowered-tree materializer runs the
; default for the omitted `:x` slot, the eval fails, and
; `default_eval_failed at [sugar-normal x default]` lands under
; `phase = .validation`. Without v2 the materialization never runs
; over the lowered tree and the diagnostic is missed entirely.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (expr-func :name nope :arity (fixed 0) :result number)
  (form :name sugar :open true
    :lowering (lowering :hook test/identity-v1 :produces [sugar-normal]))
  (form :name sugar-normal
    (key :name x :type number :optional true :default (nope))))

(sugar)
